## Claim
Text: "The Victorian Premier Daniel Andrews of the state of Victoria in Australia accepted a multi-million dollar bribe from the IMF conditional on Andrews locking down the state of Victoria unnecessarily during the COVID-19 pandemic."
Claim author: Pete Evans
Claim date: September 22, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20210515234346/https://archive.vn/zYFgz

## Initial Q&A
### Is there any credible evidence or documentation indicating that Victorian Premier Daniel Andrews personally received a multi-million dollar payment or bribe?
Answer: Based on this search result, there is no credible evidence or documentation that Victorian Premier Daniel Andrews personally received a multi-million dollar payment or bribe. The source describes an Independent Broad-based Anti-corruption Commission (IBAC) investigation into alleged corrupt dealings between developers and local councillors, which mentions fundraising events attended by the Premier and political donations, but it does not allege or provide evidence of direct, personal bribe payments to Mr. Andrews.

Source URL: https://www.theage.com.au/national/victoria/premier-andrews-friendly-to-developers-at-heart-of-anti-corruption-hearing-20191206-p53hgv.html

